  "goodToKnow": "Das Kopftuch is a headscarf: ein Kopftuch tragen. For decades rural German women wore Kopftücher too, but today the word is mostly linked to the Muslim headscarf and a long-running debate. Germany's Constitutional Court has ruled several times on whether states may ban teachers or judges from wearing one; blanket bans for teachers were ruled unconstitutional in 2015. Das Tuch means cloth or scarf. Plural: die Kopftücher."
